I can conceptually solve the Tower of Hanoi for an infinite number of disks using only recursion, conditionals, and a basic move function, as shown in this minimal form:
def hanoi(n, src, dst, aux): if n > 0: hanoi(n-1, src, aux, dst); print(f"Move disk from {src} to {dst}"); hanoi(n-1, aux, dst, src)
